<h3 data-start=3D"2916" data-end=3D"2959" class=3D"">2.4 Complexit=C3=A9 de=
 la Recherche Lin=C3=A9aire</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2961" data-end=3D"3402">
<li data-start=3D"2961" data-end=3D"3190" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2963" data-end=3D"3190" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
963" data-end=3D"2985">Temps (complexit=C3=A9)</strong> : La recherche lin=
=C3=A9aire a une <strong data-start=3D"3016" data-end=3D"3039">complexit=C3=
=A9 de temps</strong> de <strong data-start=3D"3043" data-end=3D"3051">O(n)=
</strong>, o=C3=B9 <code data-start=3D"3056" data-end=3D"3059">n</code> est=
 le nombre d'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ments dans la collection. Dans le pire des cas, l=
'algorithme doit parcourir tous les =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments de la collection.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3194" data-end=3D"3402" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3196" data-end=3D"3402" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
196" data-end=3D"3219">Espace (complexit=C3=A9)</strong> : La <strong data-=
start=3D"3225" data-end=3D"3248">complexit=C3=A9 spatiale</strong> est de <=
strong data-start=3D"3256" data-end=3D"3264">O(1)</strong>, car la recherch=
e lin=C3=A9aire ne n=C3=A9cessite qu'un nombre constant d'op=C3=A9rations s=
uppl=C3=A9mentaires, ind=C3=A9pendamment de la taille de la collection.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3404" data-end=3D"3438" class=3D"">2.5 Avantages et Incon=
v=C3=A9nients</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3440" data-end=3D"3851">
<li data-start=3D"3440" data-end=3D"3611" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3442" data-end=3D"3457" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
442" data-end=3D"3455">Avantages</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3460" data-end=3D"3611">
<li data-start=3D"3460" data-end=3D"3483" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3462" data-end=3D"3483" class=3D"">Facile =C3=A0 impl=C3=
=A9menter.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3486" data-end=3D"3543" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3488" data-end=3D"3543" class=3D"">Ne n=C3=A9cessite aucun=
e organisation pr=C3=A9alable des donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3546" data-end=3D"3608" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3548" data-end=3D"3608" class=3D"">Utile pour des petites =
collections ou des listes non tri=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3612" data-end=3D"3851" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3614" data-end=3D"3633" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
614" data-end=3D"3631">Inconv=C3=A9nients</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3636" data-end=3D"3851">
<li data-start=3D"3636" data-end=3D"3727" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3638" data-end=3D"3727" class=3D"">Lente pour des grandes =
collections de donn=C3=A9es, car elle doit parcourir tous les =C3=A9l=C3=A9=
ments.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3730" data-end=3D"3851" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3732" data-end=3D"3851" class=3D"">Inefficace par rapport =
=C3=A0 d'autres algorithmes, comme la recherche binaire, lorsque la taille =
de la collection augmente.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3853" data-end=3D"3856" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3858" data-end=3D"3884" class=3D"">=F0=9F=94=8D 3. Recher=
che Binaire</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"3886" data-end=3D"3906" class=3D"">3.1 Pr=C3=A9sentation<=
/h3>
<p data-start=3D"3908" data-end=3D"4263" class=3D"">La <strong data-start=
=3D"3911" data-end=3D"3932">recherche binaire</strong> est un algorithme be=
aucoup plus efficace, mais il n=C3=A9cessite que la collection soit <strong=
 data-start=3D"4016" data-end=3D"4025">tri=C3=A9e</strong> au pr=C3=A9alabl=
e. Contrairement =C3=A0 la recherche lin=C3=A9aire qui explore chaque =C3=
=A9l=C3=A9ment, la recherche binaire divise la collection en deux parties =
=C3=A9gales =C3=A0 chaque =C3=A9tape, ce qui permet de r=C3=A9duire de mani=
=C3=A8re significative le nombre de comparaisons.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4265" data-end=3D"4287" class=3D"">3.2 Fonctionnement</h3=
>
<p data-start=3D"4289" data-end=3D"4336" class=3D"">Voici comment fonctionn=
e la recherche binaire :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"4337" data-end=3D"4800">
<li data-start=3D"4337" data-end=3D"4396" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4340" data-end=3D"4396" class=3D"">Triez d'abord la collec=
tion (si elle ne l'est pas d=C3=A9j=C3=A0).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4397" data-end=3D"4655" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4400" data-end=3D"4471" class=3D"">Comparez l'=C3=A9l=C3=
=A9ment recherch=C3=A9 avec l'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment du milieu de la collection.=
</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4475" data-end=3D"4655">
<li data-start=3D"4475" data-end=3D"4563" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4477" data-end=3D"4563" class=3D"">Si l'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment =
recherch=C3=A9 est plus petit, la recherche se poursuit dans la moiti=C3=A9=
 gauche.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4567" data-end=3D"4655" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4569" data-end=3D"4655" class=3D"">Si l'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment =
recherch=C3=A9 est plus grand, la recherche se poursuit dans la moiti=C3=A9=
 droite.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4656" data-end=3D"4800" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4659" data-end=3D"4800" class=3D"">R=C3=A9p=C3=A9tez ces =
=C3=A9tapes jusqu'=C3=A0 ce que l'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment soit trouv=C3=A9 ou que=
 la taille de la collection =C3=A0 examiner devienne nulle (l'=C3=A9l=C3=A9=
ment n'existe pas).</p>
</li>
</ol>
