<h2 data-start=3D"4042" data-end=3D"4123" class=3D"">=F0=9F=A7=91=E2=80=8D=
=F0=9F=92=BB 4. Cas Avanc=C3=A9s : Utilisation de <code data-start=3D"4083"=
 data-end=3D"4092">super()</code> dans des Hi=C3=A9rarchies Complexes</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4125" data-end=3D"4152" class=3D"">4.1 L'H=C3=A9ritage Mu=
ltiple</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4154" data-end=3D"4412" class=3D"">Python permet l'h=C3=A9=
ritage multiple, ce qui signifie qu'une classe peut h=C3=A9riter de plusieu=
rs classes parentes. Cela peut cr=C3=A9er des situations complexes o=C3=B9 =
<code data-start=3D"4307" data-end=3D"4316">super()</code> doit =C3=AAtre u=
tilis=C3=A9 pour =C3=A9viter les conflits entre les m=C3=A9thodes des diff=
=C3=A9rentes classes parentes.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"4414" data-end=3D"4448" class=3D"">Exemple d'H=C3=A9ritag=
e Multiple :</h4>
<pre class=3D"overflow-visible!" data-start=3D"4450" data-end=3D"5059"><div=
 class=3D"contain-inline-size rounded-md border-[0.5px] border-token-border=
-medium relative bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary"><div class=3D"flex items=
